==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{LL.}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|gibbus||lang=la|hump" or "humped}}, probably cognate with ''[[cubare]]'' "to bend oneself, lie down," Italian ''[[gobba]]'' "[[humpback]]," Greek [[κύφος]] (''kyphos'') "[[humpback]], [[bent]],"  [[κύβος]] (''kybos'') "[[cube]], [[vertebra]]".

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪbəs}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by [[convex|convexity]]; [[protuberant]].
# {{astronomy}} Phase of [[moon]] between first quarter and full or between full and last [[quarter]].
# [[humpback|Humpbacked]].

